# {{ project_name }}

A generated FastAPI and LangGraph starter application created with Agentic AI
Scaffold. It provides an asynchronous webhook boundary and a small conversation
graph that can be adapted to a specific product and delivery channel.

> [!NOTE]
> This repository is a starting point. Authentication, durable processing,
> response delivery, deployment configuration, and integration tests must be
> designed for the target environment.

## Included components

- FastAPI health and message-ingestion endpoints
- LangGraph conversation state and routing
- Groq and Gemini chat-model adapters
- Pydantic Settings configuration
{% if has_db %}
- Async SQLAlchemy engine, sessions, and persistence-model package
{% endif %}
{% if has_mcp %}
- FastMCP stdio server with an example system-time tool
{% endif %}
{% if has_observability %}
- Opik configuration and tracing helpers
{% endif %}
{% if has_pre_commit %}
- Ruff linting and formatting hooks through pre-commit
{% else %}
- Ruff linting and formatting commands
{% endif %}

## Architecture

```text
src/
├── main.py                         # FastAPI entry point
├── app/
│   ├── agent/                      # LangGraph state, nodes, and routing
│   ├── gateway/api/v1/             # Versioned HTTP boundary
{% if has_mcp %}
│   └── mcp_server/                 # Optional FastMCP process
{% endif %}
└── shared/
    ├── domain/                     # Settings and shared domain types
    └── infrastructure/
{% if has_db %}
        ├── db/                     # SQLAlchemy engine, sessions, models
{% endif %}
{% if has_observability %}
        └── observability/          # Opik setup helpers
{% endif %}
```

`POST /api/v1/webhooks/message` validates a generic message, returns HTTP 202,
and schedules the LangGraph invocation as an in-process background task. The
generated task logs the model response; it does not persist or deliver it.

{% if has_mcp %}
The MCP server is independently runnable. The generated agent client currently
uses a local fallback LangChain tool and does not connect to the server. Add the
appropriate stdio or network transport before relying on remote tool discovery.
{% endif %}

