## Setup

Install the locked dependencies:

```bash
uv sync
```

Create a local configuration file:

```bash
# macOS/Linux
cp .env.example .env
```

```cmd
:: Windows CMD
copy .env.example .env
```

Replace only the values required for the integrations you use. Never commit
the resulting `.env` file.

## Run the application

Start the API from the project root:

```bash
uv run uvicorn main:app --app-dir src --reload
```

Available interfaces:

| Method | Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/` | Basic application health response |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/webhooks/message` | Accept a normalized message for background processing |
| `GET` | `/docs` | FastAPI-generated OpenAPI interface |

Example development request:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/webhooks/message \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"sender_id":"local-user","channel":"web","text_content":"Hello"}'
```

{% if has_mcp %}
Run the example MCP server in a separate terminal:

```bash
cd src
uv run python -m app.mcp_server.server
```
{% endif %}

## Configuration

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_NAME` | No | Display name used by FastAPI |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | No | Environment label; defaults to `development` |
| `ENABLE_DEBUG_LOGS` | No | Enables verbose application logging |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | No | JSON list or comma-separated browser origins |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | For Groq calls | Provider credential stored as a secret value |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | For Gemini calls | Provider credential stored as a secret value |
{% if has_db %}
| `DATABASE_URL` | For database startup | Async PostgreSQL SQLAlchemy URL |
{% endif %}
{% if has_observability %}
| `OPIK_API_KEY` | For Opik | Opik credential |
| `OPIK_WORKSPACE` | For Opik | Target workspace |
| `OPIK_PROJECT_NAME` | No | Tracing project name |
{% endif %}

The current conversation node selects Groq by default. Change
`src/app/agent/nodes.py` to make provider selection application-driven.

{% if has_db %}
## Persistence models

Place SQLAlchemy declarative mappings in
`src/shared/infrastructure/db/models/`. Import mappings from that package when
metadata or future migration tooling needs deterministic model registration.
Keep framework-independent domain types in `src/shared/domain/`.

This scaffold does not generate Alembic configuration or application tables.
{% endif %}

{% if has_observability %}
## Observability

`src/shared/infrastructure/observability/opik_setup.py` provides initialization
and tracing helpers. They are not called automatically. Initialize Opik during
the application lifespan and apply tracing to the operations your application
needs before expecting telemetry.
{% endif %}

